 "decisions": {
  "FTF-scope": "user 11-05 20:5x step 1: the FT-cap train / valid caps are removed; every structure that passes the finetune.Pool filters (level label, finite, even electron count, fmax <= 10 eV/A, exact-duplicate dedupe FT-dedupe, D0 holdout FT-d0hold, truncated Nurion systems FT-leak-trunc) is used. The pilot / capped models are not retrained; their split files and models are not touched.",
  "FTF-split": "membership = finetune.build_split unchanged (drop by tags OR targets(); validation = whole fold_core groups in a seeded order until >= 10 % of the remaining D1 reactions, + Nurion non-target rows of those cores; test = dropped structures whose rxn_ids are all held out) with caps train 0 / valid 0 (no cap) / test 20,000 (FT-cap tier rule and seed). Validation is NOT capped: the existing validation logic has no size limit besides FT-cap (FT_all_s0 had 81,569 validation structures before the cap, fold 4 41,739). Seeds = the capped runs' (valid SEED+100+k / +200+i / +300+d; cap SEED+1000+same), so FT_<k>_full holds out exactly fold k as FT_<k>. Index files = sorted int32 store row ids.",
  "FTF-g4": "G-4 (kind al_ts, $MLT/dft/gen_G4.extxyz) is included iff the file exists and results/G4_report.json says complete at data-build time (finetune with_al rules: G4 read last, dedupe after the base inputs, hold_al, tier 1); otherwise 'G-4 not used' is recorded. A running training keeps its pinned split.",
  "FTF-train": "AIMNet2 as finetune.train_aimnet: released aimnet2_wb97m_d3_0 weights (parity check vs the yaml build), atomic shifts zeroed, NaN species rows of afv -> 0, D3 head = B3LYP-D3(BJ) (s8 1.9889, a1 0.3981, a2 4.4211), molecular charge input, E0 (SAE) by least squares on <= 40,000 training structures (all with a rare element), MTLoss energy_loss_fn (ew 1) + peratom_loss_fn forces (fw), RAdam wd 1e-8 (shifts 0), batch 64, torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_value_ 0.4 (the existing value: element-wise value clipping, not norm). Loader: per epoch the shards in a seeded order (rng [train_seed, epoch]); a shard's training rows are gathered from the memory-mapped .npy files (next shard prefetched in a thread), sorted by atom count after a seeded shuffle, cut into batches of <= 64 (padding to the batch maximum, numbers 0 = padding as aimnet merge_groups), batch order shuffled. Validation rows are gathered once (exact-size batches of 128, as before).",
  "FTF-ema": "weight EMA 0.99 updated after every optimizer step (all parameters incl. shifts; torch._foreach_lerp_); validation and the exported model use the EMA weights; best_ema.pt = EMA weights of the best epoch.",
  "FTF-sched": "metric = validation force MAE over all validation structures (kcal/mol/A, mean |dF| over Cartesian components of real atoms) with EMA weights; it drives ReduceLROnPlateau (factor 0.8, patience 10, threshold 0 rel = strictly lower), best-checkpoint selection (strictly lower) and early stopping, so all three share one improvement definition. Validation energy MAE (training frame, kcal/mol) and TS-near force MAE are recorded only. Warmup: epochs 0-2, lr linear per optimizer step 1e-5 -> 1e-4; the plateau scheduler steps from epoch 3 on.",
  "FTF-stop": "stop when lr < 1e-6 after a scheduler step, or 100 epochs without a better validation force MAE, or 1,000 epochs, or the GPU-h cap; then export the best EMA weights (stop.json keeps the reason so a resubmit goes straight to export).",
  "FTF-budget": "GPU-h = wall-h of the train command (finetune.Budget, budget.json, summed over attempts). For *_full runs the 12 h target / 24 GPU-h STOP of FT-budget is replaced by a 150 GPU-h cap (user 11-05 20:5x): no epoch is started when it would end past 150 GPU-h, and a cap reached mid-epoch drops that epoch; both are a normal stop (export, exit 0), not exit 3.",
  "FTF-fw": "force weight: --fw if given; else the lead's $MLT/pipeline/ft_abl_choice.json ('fw', or 'choice' -> baseline 0.2 / fw1 1.0 / fw5 5.0); else PIPELINE_STATE.json params ft_abl_choice / ft_train_args (when ft_abl_cand is AIMNet2); else 1.0 (no FT-abl decision). The value is pinned in run_key.json at the first start; a later decision is recorded but does not change a started run (restart = --force).",
  "FTF-resume": "checkpoint every epoch (last.pt: model, EMA, optimizer, scheduler, epoch, optimizer step, best metric / epoch, the best EMA weights themselves, history; atomic; best_ema.pt is rewritten from that copy after last.pt, and again right before export, so weights and recorded best epoch always agree). lock.json is released on every exit. A resubmit resumes; the run key (split fingerprint, store, lr, ew, fw, batch, EMA) is pinned, a different key = STOP (--force moves the run dir aside, never deletes). The trainer pauses (exit 2) when the next epoch would end past --wall-h of this job.",
  "FTF-selfcheck": "at every start: split meta (C-2 pass, inputs complete, store fingerprint), index overlap, the first training shard (atom count, elements, finite arrays), one training batch forward + backward (finite loss and gradients, no optimizer step) and one validation batch with the EMA model (finite energies / forces); any failure = STOP (exit 3) before the E0 fit and training."
